                                "sense_id": "6228c9b6-f90a-3e91-85c7-b26d113526aa",
                                "text": "Prenatal exposure of the neonate to cocaine can be associated with severe defects of gastro-intestinal tract, such as necrotizing enterocolitis (43-45) and enterorrhexis (46), which are due to vasoconstriction, because of the general hypoxia and ischaemia of the fetus."
                            },
